# ReadRead sync service configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env` beside this file. Read by both the web service and `bin/readread-sync`, so the
# database path is stated once rather than repeated in the web server config and every cron line.
#
# `#` starts a comment only at the start of a line — an unquoted value runs to the end of the line,
# because these are filesystem paths.
#
# Anything already set in the process environment wins over this file, so a one-off override still
# works: READREAD_SYNC_DB=/tmp/scratch.sqlite ./bin/readread-sync status

# Where the SQLite database lives. Put it OUTSIDE the document root if you can: the shipped
# .htaccess denies it over HTTP, but a path the web server cannot reach at all is a stronger
# guarantee than a rule that has to keep working.
#
# Defaults to server/data/sync.sqlite when unset.
#READREAD_SYNC_DB=/var/lib/readread-sync/sync.sqlite
